    <h2>Dependents.</h2>
    <p>A personal representative of an estate can be an executor, administrator, or anyone who is in charge of the estate. A personal representative is the person who did during the year, you may have to file a final return for the decedent. You also have other duties, such as notifying the IRS that you are acting as the personal representative. Form <span data-field="form_number_1">{{ form_number_1 }}</span>, Notice Concerning Fiduciary Relationship, is available for free. For more information, see Publication <span data-field="publication_number_1">{{ publication_number_1 }}</span>, Survivors, Executors, and Administrators.</p>
    <p>When you file a return for the decedent, either as the personal representative or as the surviving spouse, you should write "DECEASED" in the decedent's name, and the date of death, across the top of the tax return.</p>
    <p>If no personal representative has been appointed by the court, you may file a return for the decedent, but you must notify the IRS of your role. For more information, see Publication <span data-field="publication_number_2">{{ publication_number_2 }}</span>.</p>
