      <h2>Taxable and Nontaxable Income</h2>
      <p>Generally, all income is taxable unless it is specifically exempted by law. Your taxable income may include compensation for services, interest, dividends, rents, royalties, and other forms of income. Some income, gain from sales or exchanges of property, and business income all of kinds.</p>
      <p>Under special provisions of the law, certain items are not taxable, or are only partially taxable. These are discussed in this section.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <p>2) Qualified plan if you are age 75 or older on your annuity starting date and your annuity payments are guaranteed for at least 5 years.</p>
      <p>In addition, you must meet the General Rule for payments from a qualified plan if your annuity starting date is after July 1, 1986, and before November 19, 1996, and you did not choose to use the Simplified Method. If you are age 75 or older, you may use the Simplified Method.</p>
      <p>Complete information on the General Rule, including the tables you need, is contained in Publication <span data-field="publication_number_3">{{ publication_number_3 }}</span>.</p>
